{"id": "tea:wheel-of-sharp-weapons:peacock", "source": "src:wheel-of-sharp-weapons", "location": {"ref": "peacock"}, "paraphrase": "As peacocks roam the forest of poisonous plants and thrive on poison where other birds would die, so bodhisattvas remain in the jungle of saṃsāra and turn the poisonous afflictions into the path.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "teachers": ["tch:dharmaraksita-lojong"], "practices": ["prc:lojong", "prc:taking-adversity-as-path"], "notes": "Section-level ref (the opening simile); verse numbers not recalled.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:wheel-of-sharp-weapons:wheel", "source": "src:wheel-of-sharp-weapons", "location": {"ref": "wheel"}, "paraphrase": "Whatever misfortune befalls one is the wheel of sharp weapons of one's own wrong deeds turning back upon oneself; so turn the weapon on the true enemy, the demon of self-grasping and self-cherishing, and trample it.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation", "action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:dharmaraksita-lojong"], "practices": ["prc:lojong"], "obstacles": ["obs:self-cherishing"], "concepts": ["cpt:karma-lojong"], "notes": "Paraphrase of the poem's refrain-theme; verse numbers not recalled.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
